Rules I had been working on before I gave up on the Subreddit...
--------------------------------------------------------------------

 Subreddit rules:
 
1. Keep it civil.
1. Stick to the topic of AutoHotkey.
1. No scripts that give a competitive advantage against another human.
    - This is not limited to games.
1. No requesting scripts. The privilege has been abused.
1. You must disclose when AI code is being used and you must be trying to learn the language.
    - We are not here to fix AI code for people not learning the language. That's the same as requesting a script.
1. Posts must have correct flair.
1. v1 is the deprecated version of AHK.
    - Unless there's a good reason for v1, 
    - If asking for v1 help, please provide why v1 is being used.
1. Code must be [formatted correctly]().
    - Script Help posts should contain the code or a link to the code you're having problems with.
1. Script help posts need to include code or a link to the code.
    - Consider only posting the relevant section.
1. Do not use AI to generate code or responses to people's questions.
1. Please don't delete your post afterward as it won't be searchable.
    - This makes it harder for others to find answers to similar questions.





